 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: Training time scales linearly with the number of iterations and the number of samples per ray ($N_c + N_f$) [G]. Quadrupling the sampling resolution (e.g., from 32x32 to 64x64 in NeTF context) quadruples training time [S2].
-*   **Memory Complexity**: Memory usage is dominated by the MLP weights and the intermediate activations during the forward pass [G]. Chunking (e.g., 4096 points) limits peak memory usage [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Measured Performance**:
-    *   On Blender dataset (Lego scene, 200k iterations): PSNR ~31-32 dB, SSIM ~0.96, Time ~12-15 hours on a single GPU [S3, unofficial].
-    *   With 256 hidden units: 0.84M params, 1.86 hours training time, PSNR 32.96 [S1].
-    *   With 512 hidden units: 3.23M params, 3.42 hours training time, PSNR 33.25 [S1].
-    *   Comparison: The proposed model (with proposal networks) is significantly faster to train than mip-NeRF, with speedup increasing as model capacity rises [S1].
-*   **Strengths**: Simple to implement, robust baseline, good quality on synthetic data [G].
-*   **Limitations**: Slow training for large scenes, requires many samples for high quality, sensitive to near/far plane selection [G].
